\subsection{Benchmark: Michell cantilever}
The performance of the \deHomTop code is benchmarked to the first proposed dehomogenisation for manufacturable designs \citep{Groen2018} by considering the Michell cantilever. The FE-model of the Michell cantilever can be included in the code by replacing \texttt{prepFEA()} with \texttt{prepFEA\_cant()}. 
%
The Poisson's ratio is set to $\nu = 0.3$ (line 6) in accordance with ~\cite{Groen2018}.
\begin{lstlisting}[firstnumber=6,columns=fullflexible]
[E,EMin,nu] = deal(1,1e-9,0.3); 
\end{lstlisting}
The \deHomTop code is executed with,
