deHomTop808(80,40,0.5,1.5,0.1,1,0.2,0,true);
\end{lstlisting}
where $d_{\min} = 0.2$ and $w_{\min} = 0.1$ corresponds to a mapped cell size and feature size of $40 h_f$ and $2 h_f$ \citep{Groen2018}, respectively. To best replicate the numerical setup in \cite{Groen2018}, by ensuring consistent mapping grid resolutions, the minimum thickness for \deHomTop is increased to $w_{\min} = 0.1$ compared to $w_{\min} = 0.05$ in \cite{Groen2018}.
%Note that in \cite{Groen2018}, a minimum thickness was set at $w_{\min} = 0.05$, which will for the \deHomTop implementation result in a mapping grid twice as fine, hence to replicate the numerical setup best, the size of the minimum thickness is increased. 


