\subsection{Evaluation metrics}

\textbf{MS-SSIM, LD and AD.} Our evaluation employs metrics widely used in prior research \cite{Ma2018DocUNetDI, Feng2021DocTrDI, Feng2021DocScannerRD, Zhang2022MariorMR, Jiang2022RevisitingDI, Feng2022GeometricRL, Ma2022LearningFD, Li2023ForegroundAT, feng2023doctrp, Li2023LayoutawareSD}. Structural Similarity (SSIM) assesses the similarity between two images based on their luminance, contrast, and structural attributes. Multi-Scale Structural Similarity (MS-SSIM) \cite{Wang2004ImageQA} enhances SSIM by evaluating contrast and structure across multiple scales and measuring luminance only at the final scale. Local Distortion (LD) \cite{You2016MultiviewRO} quantifies the average local deformation per pixel between the corrected image and an authentic scanned counterpart, utilizing SIFT flow \cite{Liu2011SIFTFD} for analysis. Aligned Distortion (AD) \cite{Ma2022LearningFD}, building on MS-SSIM and LD, addresses their limitations: MS-SSIM's sensitivity to minor global changes and LD's tendency to inaccurately flag errors in texture-lacking regions.

\textbf{ED and CER. }Our method's dewarping quality on distorted images is assessed using OCR recognition performance. Edit Distance (ED) is defined as the minimum number of operations needed to transform one string into another, including insertions (\textit{i}), deletions (\textit{d}), and substitutions (\textit{s}). Consequently, the Character Error Rate (CER) is calculated using the formula: ($\textit{i} + \textit{d} + \textit{s}) / \textit{M}$, where \textit{M} represents the total number of characters in the reference string. In alignment with previous methodologies \cite{Feng2021DocTrDI, Feng2022GeometricRL, Li2023ForegroundAT, Li2023LayoutawareSD}, our evaluation on the DocUNet Benchmark involves 50 and 60 images, respectively. Furthermore, the DIR300 dataset's OCR performance is analyzed using 90 text-rich images, maintaining consistency with these established methods. The CER and ED performance of all 200 images are displayed on the DocReal benchmark.

