\subsection{Implementation details}

During training, input images are cropped and then resized to $448 \times 448$. Optimization is performed using the AdamW optimizer \cite{Loshchilov2017DecoupledWD}, with a batch size set to 28. The learning rate begins at a maximum of $1\times 10^{-4}$ and decreases to a minimum of $1\times 10^{-7}$, employing a cosine learning rate decay strategy. The model undergoes training for 80 epochs with a warm-up phase of 10,000 steps. Following \cite{Feng2021DocTrDI, Zhang2022MariorMR, Feng2022GeometricRL, Feng2021DocScannerRD, Li2023LayoutawareSD}, evaluation metrics MS-SSIM, LD, and AD are computed using Matlab R2019a. OCR performance assessment on the two English benchmarks DocUNet and DIR300 are conducted using Tesseract v5.0.1.2022011 \cite{Smith2007AnOO} with pytesseract v0.3.8 \footnote{https://pypi.org/project/pytesseract/}. Since PaddleOCR is open source and available, and has shown excellent performance in Chinese text recognition, we use it for evaluation on the Chinese benchmark DocReal \cite{Yu_2024_WACV}.

