\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}

We adopt Mixed Error Rate (MER) as evaluation metric to assess model performance on code-switching speech recognition tasks. MER computes character error rate (CER) for Mandarin segments and word error rate (WER) for English segments, thereby aligning with the natural granularity of individual languages. 


% Formally, MER is computed as:

% \[
% \mathrm{MER} = \frac{S_w + D_w + I_w}{N_w}
% \]

% where \( S_w \), \( D_w \), and \( I_w \) denote the number of substitutions, deletions, and insertions respectively, and \( N_w \) is the total number of words in the reference transcript. In the case of mixed-language transcripts, language-aware alignment is applied to avoid over-penalizing transliterations or semantically equivalent substitutions between languages.



