\subsection{Formal Validation and Integration}

To validate the correctness and relevance of generated assertions, we integrate formal verification tools such as Cadence JasperGold into our evaluation pipeline:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Syntactic Validation}:  
    Assertions are first checked for syntactic correctness and type consistency to ensure compatibility with SystemVerilog Assertion (SVA) standards.

    \item \textbf{Formal Property Proving}:  
    For syntactically valid assertions, bounded model checking and formal proof engines are employed to determine whether each assertion is vacuously true, violated, or non-provable within the RTL design.
\end{itemize}

Assertion pass rates and violation traces are collected as quantitative metrics, enabling both automated assessment and refinement. This validation step ensures that the generated assertions are not only structurally significant but also practically meaningful.

\subsection{Summary}

By extending assertion evaluation to handle complex multi-signal consequents and incorporating spatial-temporal characteristics, our assertion evaluation framework provides a effective approach for identifying critical assertions. Integration with formal verification further strengthens the robustness and practical relevance of the evaluation process, ultimately advancing the state-of-the-art in specification-driven verification.

