The main contributions of this paper are as follows: (1) an approach for discovering stochastic Petri nets from social network event data; (2) methods for analyzing and categorizing AI and human agent behavior based on the discovered stochastic Petri net models; (3) the application of the proposed techniques to real-world social network data to identify coordinated online behaviors.

