The goal is usually to have linear construction time.
To achieve this, it is always possible to partition the input to smaller MPHFs.
However, partitioning comes with a performance penalty, both during construction and query.
\Cref{fig:scalingN} starts at rather small input sets of 1~million keys and goes all the way up to 200 million.
