\myparagraph{Construction\@.}
Overall, the ARM machine is slower, which can be explained by the fact that it is a server machine with lower base clock speed.
On the ARM machine, Bip. ShockHash-Flat is Pareto optimal mainly because ShockHash gets slower.
The reason for this is that the splittings profit most from SIMD parallelism, and the approaches do not have an ARM implementation.
This is also the reason why SIMDRecSplit is missing completely.
The construction throughput of FiPS surpasses the one of PtrHash, in contrast to the Intel machine.

\myparagraph{Queries\@.}
In terms of query throughput, all approaches are slower on the ARM machine as well.
However, PTHash and PHOBIC are impacted most, showing smaller queries even in comparison to other approaches.

