\subparagraph*{Organization of the paper.}
In Section~\ref{sec:problem}, we start with a formal problem definition. Then, in Section~\ref{sec:feasible} we will first characterize feasible instances by providing necessary conditions and then present all cases where instances with a directed symmetric tree topology can be easily solved. 
We will also discuss in more detail the special case of a given period $\Delta = 2$. 
In Section~\ref{sec:hardness}, we give our hardness results for the remaining instances with a directed symmetric tree topology. Finally, we conclude in Section~\ref{sec:conclusions} with a summary and suggestions for future work.

