\section{TPF, functional level. A class of in-context learning tasks: templatic generation \label{sec:fun}}
%%
Thus the \swap\ task implicitly incorporates 11 of the 13 properties of symbolic computation given in (\ref{ex:props}).%
\footnote{
Higher-level compositionality (\ref{ex:compos}) across multiple templates given through multiple examples in the prompt, and recursion (\ref{ex:recur}), are important properties to be incorporated in future work: see the preliminary discussion in Sec.~\ref{sec:compRec}.
}
This motivates the study of a class \F\ of ICL functions including \swap\ which we formalize in this section.
\F\ provides the functional-level description of the Transformer Production Framework TPF we now develop.
We call \F\ \textit{templatic generation} tasks: \textit{TGT}.
