\subsection{Generation algorithm GEN in the Production-System Language PSL   \label{sec:GENPSL}  }
In Sec.~\ref{sec:GenAlg} we informally introduced the two operations used during generation of the continuation string: \CF\ and \NF.
Which of these is executed depends on whether the most-recently-generated symbol is final in its field (calling for \NF) or not (calling for \CF).

\subsubsection{\CF   \label{sec:contfield} }
