\end{figure}
%%

\paragraph{Convergence} To validate the convergence results established in Theorems \ref{th:514} and \ref{th:517}, we compute the relative errors in the $\mathcal{V}_{e,\bh}(Q_T)$ norm for $(U_{\bh}, V_{\bh})$, and in the $L^2(Q_T)$ norm for $U_{\bh}$. When using splines in both space and time with equal polynomial degree $p$ and uniform mesh size $h = h_t = h_x$, Theorem~\ref{th:514} predicts a convergence rate of order $\mathcal{O}(h^p)$ in the $\mathcal{V}_{e,\bh}(Q_T)$ norm. Furthermore, from Theorem~\ref{th:517}, we expect a convergence rate of order $\mathcal{O}(h^{p+1})$ in the $L^2$ norm. These theoretical rates are confirmed numerically in Figures~\ref{fig:3} and \ref{fig:4} for both maximal regularity and $C^1$-splines. As expected, for~$\|V-V_{\bh}\|_{L^2(Q_T)}$, we obtained the same convergence rates as for~$\|U-U_{\bh}\|_{L^2(Q_T)}$. We do not report these results here, for brevity.

