\section{Confidence Measurement}

To the best of our knowledge, we are the first to utilize confidence scores to identify unreliable extraction segments in TSE outputs. As no existing annotated datasets are directly applicable, we address this challenge through a multi-step approach. We first analyze the potential target speech extraction states and then simulate a dataset with paired confidence scores to approximate the main components of real TSE outputs. Then, we train a model to predict fine-grained confidence scores with the simulated dataset. 
