To facilitate efficient buffering, we instantiate multiple reassembly buffers that operate in the following manner.
A non-empty buffer is \emph{eligible} to accept the first fragment of a new request only if it has finished reassembling any prior request it accepted fragments for, and only if the size of the new incoming request is less than the remaining space in the buffer. A buffer that is in the middle of reassembling a request or which has less space than is required for the new incoming request cannot accept it. The first fragment of a new incoming request will select among \emph{eligible} buffers based on a policy, explored in \cref{sec:simreqbuffalloc}. If there are no \emph{eligible} buffers, the incoming request fragment is dropped (as with the request's remaining fragments) and the client is notified.
