As in \cref{fig:Request-format}, we define a small 64B custom \emph{request header} that is embedded in the first segment in a request. This header identifies the \textsf{Accelerator} (2B) and the request \textsf{Size} (2B), plus 60B as the \textsf{Parameters} field that is used to pass accelerator-specific parameters, e.g., the value $K$ for the Top-K accelerator. \textsf{Parameters} is opaque to OffRAC, which passes it to the accelerator with the payload data. The size of this field (60B) is standardized to simplify our implementation but other designs are possible.

